---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BeliefList from '../components/BeliefList.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Colleen Shifflett"
  description="Ten years of analytics across financial services, SaaS, media, and government, and what I believe about websites in the AI era."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Hi, I'm Colleen.</h1>
        <p>
          I've spent ten years in analytics across financial services, B2B SaaS,
          media, and federal government. I have helped launch several web
          analytics programs from small startups to large national organizations
          and businesses. I've provided training and resources for over 500
          non-technical professionals to use their own data with confidence.
          Most recently I've enhanced my experience as an embedded analytics
          engineer, keeping my technical practice sharp in alignment with my
          creative direction.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What I believe</h2>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: var(--bca-space-8);">
        <BeliefList variant="short" />
      </div>
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Right-sized beats sophisticated.</strong> The best web program
          is the one your team can actually run. I size the plan to the people
          and hours you have, especially if that team is just you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Your team owns the work at the end.</strong> Every engagement
          ends with governance and training, so the system keeps running after
          I step back.
        </p>

        <h2>Now</h2>
        <p>
          I'm currently embedded as an analytics engineer with a national
          subscription business. That work keeps the math side of my practice
          sharp, and it means we take on a small number of Bright Cave projects
          at a time.
        </p>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: October 2026</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
